# Schemas

## Location
`shared/schemas/` — JSON Schema files for all declarative YAML artifacts.

## Schemas
| File | Validates |
|---|---|
| `shared/schemas/check.schema.json` | Check YAML definition |
| `shared/schemas/metric.schema.json` | Metric definition YAML |
| `shared/schemas/policy.schema.json` | Governance policy YAML |
| `shared/schemas/oncall-route.schema.json` | On-call routing rule YAML |

The check schema is also mirrored at `packages/dqt/src/dqt/checks/schema/check.schema.json` for library-only users.

## Validation
All YAML files are validated against the JSON Schema at load time using `jsonschema`. Invalid files raise `CheckDefinitionError` (or equivalent) immediately, not at run time.

## Schema evolution
- Additive changes (new optional fields): safe, no migration required.
- Breaking changes (required fields added, field renamed/removed): require a version bump in the schema's `$schema` URL and a migration guide in `docs/`.
- Never remove required fields without a deprecation cycle.

## OpenAPI schema
The FastAPI server's OpenAPI schema at `/openapi.json` is generated from Pydantic models. It is the source of truth for the REST API contract. `packages/dqt-types/` is generated from this schema via `make types` using `openapi-typescript`.

- The OpenAPI schema is regenerated in CI via `python -m apps.server.scripts.dump_openapi`.
- If the schema changes (new field, new endpoint), `make types` must be re-run and the generated `api.ts` is updated (but not committed — it's git-ignored).

## Check schema structure (key fields)
```jsonschema
{
  "$schema": "...",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["name", "dataset", "detector"],
  "properties": {
    "name":       { "type": "string" },
    "dataset":    { "type": "string" },
    "column":     { "type": "string" },
    "detector":   { "type": "string" },       // registered slug
    "params":     { "type": "object" },
    "baseline":   { "$ref": "#/$defs/Baseline" },
    "schedule":   { "type": "string" },       // cron expression
    "severity":   { "enum": ["warn", "fail"] },
    "group":      { "type": "string" }
  }
}
```
